  "approvals": [
    {
      "who": "Paul Robello (owner)",
      "when": "2026-10-13",
      "gate": "reference",
      "approved": [
        "assets-source/refs/road_straight/ref-1.jpg"
      ],
      "notes": "ref-1: straight two-lane asphalt road, dashed centre line, kerbs, grass verges. ref-2 not approved. Kit requirement (owner: \"we will need bent road tiles so road can change direction\"): the road profile and the edge/center design must support bent and turning road pieces later. Bent pieces are not built in P1. Reviewed in chat on a contact sheet of the approved ref images (scripts/refs/contact-sheet.mjs)."
    },
    {
      "gate": "piece",
      "status": "pending",
      "requested": "2026-10-20",
      "notes": "Pending owner review; not an approval. Review against assets-source/refs/road_straight (ref-1: 'grass verges with tufts and small bushes'): bush_verge's third variant, a flowering hawthorn-like verge bush, 1.05 m tall and about 1.0 m across (LOD0), upright with an uneven sprayed outline, a deep fresh green mass of numpy-drawn leaf-cluster cards dotted with cream-white blossom corymbs (about 15% of the outer tiles' opaque texels), cards down to the grass, plant wind data. Built on _shrub.build through _verge_bush.py and _verge_bush_c.py. Review sheet: docs/checkpoints/bush_verge_c/sheet.jpg (ref; textured EEVEE lineup with shrub_forest, bush_verge, bush_verge_b and a 1.7 m figure; the three verge bushes close and far; the kit road tile (0, 0); play shots with docs/checkpoints/bush_verge_c/integration.patch applied). The controller records the owner's decision."
    },
    {
      "gate": "piece",
      "status": "pending",
      "requested": "2026-10-20",
      "notes": "Pending owner review; not an approval. Seasonal blossom hook (owner 2026-10-20: 'should not blossom turning winter'): rebuilt with the ORM's A carrying 1 - blossom coverage (5.4% of the atlas), the leaves slot's manifest 'blossom' leaf and flower colours from the bake report's blossomHook. Albedo, normal, masks, the PNG ORM's RGB and the GLB are byte-identical to the previous build; the BC7/ASTC ORM re-encode with the new alpha, and kit_hooks=none renders with the old and new ORM KTX2s differ in at most 29 of 1.6 M pixels (run-to-run noise 11-21), so the summer (MVP) look is unchanged. Out of season (any season index but 0, here kit_hooks=autumn) the blossom turns to leaf before the autumn tint: docs/checkpoints/bush_verge_c/vergec-season-none.jpg, vergec-season-autumn.jpg and vergec-season-crop.jpg (kit scenario, vergec-kit.json sun camera). The controller records the owner's decision."
    },
    {
      "who": "Paul Robello (owner)",
      "when": "2026-10-20",
      "gate": "piece",
      "status": "approved",
      "notes": "Approved in chat from docs/review/2026-10-20-walkthrough.html item A6."
    },
    {
      "who": "pending (owner)",
      "when": null,
      "gate": "piece",
      "status": "pending",
      "revision": "matte-leaves",
      "requested": "2026-10-26",
      "notes": "Pending owner review; not an approval. Rebuilt for the owner's bug report (2026-10-26, \"these bushes are too shiny\"): the leaf texels' roughness (ORM G) was 0.50-0.64, glossy on the dark round mass, so the sky's specular lay across the top of the bush as a grey sheen at low play cameras. _verge_bush.py now maps it linearly onto 0.76-0.86 (mean 0.81 over the opaque texels, the grass draws at 0.78); the shade blob (0.85) and the florets (0.72) keep theirs. Only the ORM's G changed: albedo, normal and masks PNGs, the mesh, LODs, collider and sockets are byte-identical to the approved build (the albedo and normal KTX2 re-encode under the current single-threaded UASTC settings). Before and after in play: docs/checkpoints/bush-shine/sheet.jpg. The controller records the owner's decision."
    }
  ]
